Contains scripts used for:
 1) collecting and processing regression-tests output (tar files or emails)
 2) front_page building (this include making the testing page)
 3) making a daily tar file of source code

.--- Setting-up: -----------------------
On mitgcmcvs.mit.edu , as jm_c , in /home/jm_c/testing :

 Just need to put, in /home/jm_c/testing/, a copy of script "daily_update"
 https://github.com/MITgcm/regression_tests/blob/master/collect_tests/daily_update

 and to set-up the crontab according to "crontab_gcm"
 https://github.com/MITgcm/regression_tests/blob/master/collect_tests/crontab_gcm

---- Getting a working "munpack" : ------
 Since we are not able to configure & compile stuff here to generate executables
 "mpack" and "munpack", take dir "tools/mpack-1.6" (already compiled)
 from villon.mit.edu (or baudelaire.mit.edu):
 a) make a tar file of:
   jm_c@villon.mit.edu:/home/jm_c/mitgcm/gcm_current/tools/mpack-1.6/
 b) copy it here (in /home/jm_c/testing) as: "tools_mpack"
  > tar -xf tools_mpack.tar
  > mv mpack-1.6 tools_mpack"
 c) and finally:
  > ln -s tools_mpack/munpack munpack.x86_64

----------------------------------------
---- Other email settings : ------------
 Note: testreport output emails sent to: "jm_c@mitgcm.org"
       are put in ~/Mail/MITgcm-test on: jm_c@mitgcm-mm.mit.edu
       by procmail, using:
#  1) file: ~/.forward :
-----> File starts here:
"| /usr/bin/procmail"
<----- File Ends here.
#  2) file: ~/.procmailrc :
-----> File starts here:

PATH=/bin:/usr/bin
MAILDIR=$HOME/Mail      #you'd better make sure it exists
DEFAULT=$MAILDIR/default
LOGFILE=$MAILDIR/log    #recommended

#  :0 c
:0
* ^Subject:.*MITgcm-test
MITgcm-test

:0
! jmc@mit.edu

<----- File Ends here.

----------------------------------------
---- Notice on sftp server : -----------
  Content of file "README" that is kept on: sftp_shared@svante8.mit.edu:/uploads/
  as this location is used to upload some regression-test output
   (e.g., using: ./testreport -send upload_sftp -a sftp_shared@svante8.mit.edu )
-----> File starts here:
Location to upload testreport output tar-files (*.tar.gz), that will be downloaded
 (every 1/2 h) by script "prc_tr_emails" (calling: get+parse_msg) and put in place.

IMPORTANT: Should not put any "*.tar.gz" file here other than test output ones
 (from "testreport" or "do_tst_2+2") as they will be wrongly assumed to be an
 output to process, resulting in failure down the road.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<----- File Ends here.
